  "note": [
    "Scripture source: Bíblia Livre para o Mundo (porbrbsl), from the ebible mirror por_bpm (scripts/bible_mirror.py); every cited verse's text was handed to its chapter's translator, and the whole Bible was on disk for uncited quotations.",
    "Derived by measurement: a row is mined only when the translator reported the quotation verbatim AND its words (punctuation and quote marks stripped, ≥10 characters) are a substring of the porbrbsl verse and appear in the chapter. Two verbatim claims failed that (Matthew 11:29 spliced across an ellipsis; Matthew 21:9 'Hosana! Hosana!' doubled) and ship self_rendered. Citations of allusions (no quoted words) are listed self_rendered.",
    "Conventions: curly “ ” mirrored from the English; citations converted to Arabic C:V with full pt book names; the Disciple addresses the Master with capitalised Tu/Te/Ti, the Master addresses the Disciple with lower-case tu (precedent: the shipped pt Imitação de Cristo dialogue), the Master's Me/Meu capitalised as the English capitalises them; parable characters and reader-address use você.",
    "English source slips rendered as written (not fixed): (1 Sam. … v. 13-14) — 1 Samuel 5 has 12 verses; (Rev. ii. 7) for the hidden manna = Rev 2:17; (Luke ix.27,28) for 'blessed is the womb' = Luke 11:27-28; (2 Tim. iv.4, 5-8) — 4:4 is about fables."
